# Why check:all's cold-start stage saw no paint, 2026-10-15 (IST), release app built from 568168d.
# Commands and their output, in order. $TMPDIR stands for the per-user temporary folder.

## 1. Frontmost app and its full-screen state, read at 10:39 IST
$ osascript -e 'tell application "System Events" to get name of first application process whose frontmost is true'
$ osascript -e 'tell application "System Events" to get value of attribute "AXFullScreen" of window 1 of (first application process whose frontmost is true)'
Dia
true

## 2. The harness alone, with nothing activating the app (the same two reads first)
T3 Code (Nightly)
false
$ node perf/cold-start.ts --ci --out <probe dir>
warmup-1: FAIL no paint marker in 10 s (window not visible?)

## 3. Visible windows and their full-screen state
$ osascript -l JavaScript -e "<list each visible process's windows with AXFullScreen and size>"
Messages: fs=false size=1024,768
Finder: fs=false size=920,464
Terminal: fs=false size=580,385
bridge-gui: fs=false size=1080,808
Mail: fs=false size=1440,869
Lettera: fs=false size=1228,761
Dia: fs=true size=1440,900
FluidVoice: fs=false size=1197,700
Claude: fs=false size=1200,800

## 4. Launch the binary directly, as the harness does, then make it frontmost by PID (the attempt-1 watcher's method)
$ AELOMI_PERF_REPORT=$D/report.json AELOMI_DATA_DIR=$D/data Aelomi.app/Contents/MacOS/aelomi &
$ sleep 1.5
$ osascript -e 'tell application "System Events" to get {frontmost, visible, name} of (first process whose unix id is $P)'
false, true, aelomi
$ osascript -l JavaScript -e "<windows of the process with unix id $P>"
[]
$ osascript -e 'tell application "System Events" to set frontmost of (first process whose unix id is $P) to true'
$ sleep 3; ls -la $D/report.json
ls: $TMPDIR/tmp.ivIsvH9xYM/report.json: No such file or directory
$ kill -0 $P && echo still-running
still-running
$ tail -3 $D/out.log
index main_peak_rss_bytes=96845824 t_ms=236.0
ping seq=1
quit frontend ready

## 5. Launch the binary directly, then activate the app by bundle ID (the watcher used for the passing run)
$ AELOMI_PERF_REPORT=$D/report.json AELOMI_DATA_DIR=$D/data Aelomi.app/Contents/MacOS/aelomi &
$ sleep 0.8
$ osascript -e 'tell application id "com.aelomi.app" to activate'
$ ls -la $D/report.json   (polled for up to 6 s)
-rw-r--r--@ 1 <user>  staff  439 Oct 15 12:50 $TMPDIR/tmp.qf8oANy8TC/report.json
$ kill -0 $P || echo exited
exited

# Reading: no directly launched window painted its first frame, including in step 2 with T3 Code (not full screen)
# frontmost. In step 4 the frontend had started (ping seq=1, quit frontend ready), yet System Events listed no window
# for the process, and making it frontmost by PID changed nothing, so plain occlusion is ruled out. In step 5,
# activating the app by bundle ID painted the first frame, wrote the report and let the app quit. A full-screen Dia
# window held its own Space all session. Which macOS rule keeps a directly spawned app's window off screen until the
# app is activated was not established.
